# ============================================================================
# Data — large reference files, GWAS sumstats, etc. (140GB+)
# ============================================================================
data/

# ============================================================================
# Intermediate results — large matrices, npz files (1.3GB)
# Exception: the small Sst mean-expression slice + its provenance note are
# tracked, so Figure 4 is reproducible without the external enrichment repo.
# (Pattern must be `dir/*`, not `dir/`, or git will not descend to see the
#  negations below.)
# ============================================================================
results/intermediates/*
!results/intermediates/README.md
!results/intermediates/seaad_sst_supertype_mean_expression.csv
# Figure 4 (A9 rebuild): the enrichment result, the taxonomy match and the
# type-name map are small and are what r_panels/MANIFEST.tsv checksums, so
# they are tracked. The matrices they derive from (specificity 160 MB,
# Siletti cluster matrix 215 MB, pooled A9 means 81 MB) stay untracked and
# are regenerated by scripts/figures/{siletti_l2_log1p,build_spec_a9rbh}.py
!results/intermediates/T_a9rbh_bigdeli.gsa.out
!results/intermediates/franken_rbh_A9.csv
!results/intermediates/namemap_a9rbh.csv
# Figure 4 robustness supplement: the two alternative enrichment runs and
# the MTG type-name map. The specificity matrices behind them (158 MB each)
# stay untracked and are rebuilt by build_spec_mtg_sametax.py.
!results/intermediates/T_a9_pgc3.gsa.out
!results/intermediates/T_mtg_bigdeli.gsa.out
!results/intermediates/namemap_mtg_sametax.csv

